        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nNow I understand the issue. The code in the MLCommons repository uses the old librosa API. Let me check what specific changes need to be made based on the problem description:\n\n1. `librosa.filters.mel` - now requires keyword arguments\n2. `librosa.core.resample` - now expects `orig_sr` and `target_sr` as keyword arguments\n3. `librosa.effects.trim` - now uses `top_db` as keyword argument\n4. `torch.stft` - returns complex tensor by default (this is PyTorch, not librosa)\n\nLet me create a patch file to fix these issues:\n\n",
