            "output": "<path>/workspace/docker/pytorch-aarch64/patches/mlcommons_rnnt.patch</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # *******************************************************************************\n2: # Copyright 2021-2023 Arm Limited and affiliates.\n3: # SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n4: #\n5: # Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");\n6: # you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.\n7: # You may obtain a copy of the License at\n8: #\n9: #     http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n10: #\n11: # Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\n12: # distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,\n13: # WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.\n14: # See the License for the specific language governing permissions and\n15: # limitations under the License.\n16: # *******************************************************************************\n17: #\n18: # This patch file includes commit 077f823ece09e37d9d40540d8acd504bf138e880\n19: # from the MLCommons inference repository, and further additions to make\n20: # the shell scripts suitable for building and running on AArch64 systems\n21: # without Conda installed.\n22: #\n23: # *******************************************************************************\n24: diff --git a/speech_recognition/rnnt/README.md b/speech_recognition/rnnt/README.md\n25: index 27fbabd..2794bed 100644\n26: --- a/speech_recognition/rnnt/README.md\n27: +++ b/speech_recognition/rnnt/README.md\n28: @@ -4,18 +4,12 @@ character transcription, without an external language model.\n29:  \n30:  # 2. Directions\n31:  \n32: -Open `run.sh`. Set the stage variable to \"-1\". Set \"work_dir\" to a\n33: -path backed by a disk with at least 30 GB of space. Most space is used\n34: -by loadgen logs, not the data or model. You need conda and a C/C++\n35: -compiler on your PATH. I used conda 4.8.2. This script is responsible\n36: -for downloading dependencies, data, and the model.\n37: -\n38: -Run `./run.sh` from this directory. Note that stage 3 runs all of the\n39: -scenarios for the reference implementation, which will take a long\n40: -time, so you may want to exist before then.\n41: -\n42: -As you complete individual stages, you can set the variable \"stage\" to\n43: -a higher number for restarting from a later stage.\n44: +To download the dataset and model, run `download_dataset_model.sh`.\n45: +To run the model, use `run.sh`; this shell script runs the SingleStream\n46: +scenario by default if no others are specified. Use `run.sh --help` to\n47: +view the full list of available flags and a usage example. Note that\n48: +the RNNT directory will need to be a path backed by a disk with at least 30\n49: +GB of space. Most space is used by loadgen logs, not the data or model.\n50:  \n51:  # 3. Dataset/Environment\n52:  ### Publication/Attribution\n53: @@ -113,4 +107,4 @@ The differences are as follows:\n54:  ### Quality metric\n55:  7.452253714852645% Word Error Rate (WER) across all words in the output text of\n56:  all samples less than 15 seconds in length in the dev-clean set, using a greedy\n57: -decoder and a fully FP32 model.\n58: \\ No newline at end of file\n59: +decoder and a fully FP32 model.\n60: diff --git a/speech_recognition/rnnt/download_dataset_model.sh b/speech_recognition/rnnt/download_dataset_model.sh\n61: new file mode 100755\n62: index 0000000..8d4ac05\n63: --- /dev/null\n64: +++ b/speech_recognition/rnnt/download_dataset_model.sh\n65: @@ -0,0 +1,46 @@\n66: +#!/bin/bash\n67: +# *******************************************************************************\n68: +# Copyright 2021 Arm Limited and affiliates.\n69: +# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n70: +#\n71: +# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");\n72: +# you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.\n73: +# You may obtain a copy of the License at\n74: +#\n75: +#     http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n76: +#\n77: +# Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\n78: +# distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,\n79: +# WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.\n80: +# See the License for the specific language governing permissions and\n81: +# limitations under the License.\n82: +# *******************************************************************************\n83: +set -euo pipefail\n84: +\n85: +base=\"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\"\n86: +work_dir=$base/temp_work\n87: +local_data_dir=$work_dir/local_data\n88: +librispeech_download_dir=$local_data_dir/LibriSpeech\n89: +\n90: +mkdir -p $librispeech_download_dir\n91: +\n92: +# if venv not active, activate\n93: +if [[ $(python -c \"import sys; print(sys.prefix)\") != \"/home/ubuntu/python3-venv\" ]]; then\n94: +    source /home/ubuntu/python3-venv/bin/activate\n95: +fi\n96: +\n97: +# stage 0: download model. Check checksum to skip?\n98: +wget https://zenodo.org/record/3662521/files/DistributedDataParallel_1576581068.9962234-epoch-100.pt?download=1 -O $work_dir/rnnt.pt\n99: +\n100: +# stage 1: download data. This will have a non-zero exit code if the\n101: +# checksum is incorrect.\n102: +python pytorch/utils/download_librispeech.py \\\n103: +     pytorch/utils/librispeech-inference.csv \\\n104: +     $librispeech_download_dir \\\n105: +     -e $local_data_dir\n106: +\n107: +# stage 2: perform necessary conversions on data\n108: +python pytorch/utils/convert_librispeech.py \\\n109: +  --input_dir $librispeech_download_dir/dev-clean \\\n110: +  --dest_dir $local_data_dir/dev-clean-wav \\\n111: +  --output_json $local_data_dir/dev-clean-wav.json\n112: diff --git a/speech_recognition/rnnt/run.sh b/speech_recognition/rnnt/run.sh\n113: index 7538df9..d65a87c 100755\n114: --- a/speech_recognition/rnnt/run.sh\n115: +++ b/speech_recognition/rnnt/run.sh\n116: @@ -1,90 +1,108 @@\n117: -#/bin